<title>RUSSIA: Russian utility UES prefs gain 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian utility UES prefs gain 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preferred shares of Russian national utility UES (Unified Energy System), a leading stock in the market, rose 14.9 percent in a bullish market on Wednesday morning.</p>
<p>UES prefs rose to $0.2040 at 0935 GMT on the Russian Trading System (RTS) from $0.1775 at Tuesday's close. Share turnover was 3.8 million. Ordinary shares of UES rose to $0.2542 from $0.2335 on 9.4 million shares turnover.</p>
<p>The RTS index is at an all-time high.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
